<%- /*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2

Caller of the shared licence check, as a consumer keeps it in
.github/workflows/licence-check.yml. The rendered file is the whole of the
consumer's licence job: the steps live in .github/workflows/licence.yml of the
shared repository, named here by commit with the version as a comment.

Required check: "Licence". The forge reports the calling job only as
"Licence / REUSE lint". The job `result` reports "Licence" and fails unless the
call passed; the engine reads it as covering the calling job
(cordanaLLM/praetor#1212, decision record 0030). The caller passes no `root`:
a run narrowed to a folder is reported as "Licence / REUSE lint (<root>)" and
never stands in for the whole repository (decision record 0027).

On a draft the call job is skipped and the result job fails with the draft
annotation, so the required check stays red and no runner is spent until the
ready_for_review run (PR 47).

Fields: .Shared.Repository, .Shared.Commit and .Shared.Version are working
names until the engine renders caller templates (cordanaLLM/praetor#1211);
.RunnerTag is the engine's own. The trigger is spelled out for the same reason:
with the engine it becomes the hosted gate's trigger function.

Concurrency is set here and not in the shared workflow, so a consumer's group
never collides with another caller's.

Licence header: the rendered caller starts with the consumer's own header,
written from .Licence (working names, as above), so the consumer's licence
check accepts it (#3). The REUSE-IgnoreStart and REUSE-IgnoreEnd notes render
as nothing and keep this repository's licence check from reading the field
lines as tags.
*/ -%>
<%- /* REUSE-IgnoreStart */ -%>
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: <% .Licence.CopyrightText %>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: <% .Licence.Identifier %>
<%/* REUSE-IgnoreEnd */ -%>
---
# Licence check: every file carries its licence information. The job is the
# shared workflow of <% .Shared.Repository %>, named by commit.
name: Licence check

on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]
  push:
    branches: [main]
  merge_group:

permissions: {}

concurrency:
  group: licence-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

jobs:
  # A draft skips this job, and the result job below fails for it, so the
  # required check stays red on a draft until the ready_for_review run.
  licence:
    name: Licence
    if: >-
      github.event_name != 'pull_request'
      || github.event.pull_request.draft == false
    permissions:
      contents: read
    uses: <% .Shared.Repository %>/.github/workflows/licence.yml@<% .Shared.Commit %> # <% .Shared.Version %>
    with:
      runner: <% .RunnerTag %>

  # The forge reports the calling job above only as "Licence / REUSE lint",
  # never as "Licence", so a rule set that requires "Licence" waits forever.
  # This job reports "Licence" and fails unless the licence check passed; it
  # runs under always() so a failed, cancelled or skipped check still reports
  # here.
  result:
    name: Licence
    needs: licence
    if: always()
    runs-on: <% .RunnerTag %>
    timeout-minutes: 5
    permissions: {}
    steps:
      # yamllint disable rule:line-length
      - name: Report the draft
        if: needs.licence.result == 'skipped'
        shell: bash
        run: |
          echo "::error title=Gate not run on a draft::The gate did not run because the pull request is a draft. It runs when the pull request is marked ready for review."
          exit 1
      # yamllint enable rule:line-length
      - name: Fail unless the licence check passed
        if: needs.licence.result != 'success'
        shell: bash
        run: |
          echo "The licence check did not pass or was skipped on a draft."
          exit 1
